// Distributed 2D-grid schedule: 4 compute workers in a 2x2 grid via
// `partition=blocks2d` over the outer (i, j) nest of the matmul
// triple loop. Host runs load/save. The innermost `k` loop is the
// reduction axis and is NOT partitioned.
//
// M5 AC#4 follow-up to 07-matmul/distributed (TASK-0297 +
// TASK-0301). This cell discharges the 2D shape of TASK-0302
// (`wait_slice` axis-mapping under sparse partition coverage).
//
// Partition shape
// ---------------
// `loop i : partition=blocks2d;` pairs the outer i-loop with the
// inner j-loop into a 2x2 worker grid (per partition_blocks2d's
// decompose_grid(4) = (2,2)). N=16, 2 rows × 2 cols → i_band = 8,
// j_band = 8 per worker. Each worker computes
//     c[i_band][j_band] = sum_k a[i_band][k] * b[k][j_band]
//
// Per-worker assignment (row-major over BTreeSet numeric WorkerId
// order — matches partition_blocks2d.rs's `for (i, wid) in
// body_workers.iter().enumerate() { row = i / cols; col = i % cols }`):
//     w0 (0,0): i=0..8,  j=0..8     w1 (0,1): i=0..8,  j=8..16
//     w2 (1,0): i=8..16, j=0..8     w3 (1,1): i=8..16, j=8..16
//
// Why this is bit-identical with naive/blocked/distributed
// --------------------------------------------------------
// The k-accumulator semantics are unchanged under the (i, j)
// partition: each output c[i][j] is the SAME sum over k = 0..N
// regardless of which worker computes it. Workers are independent
// on (i, j); no halo, no cross-worker carry, no reduction across
// (i, j). The existing reference.bin oracle applies — no new
// reference is needed.
//
// Why this needs TASK-0302
// ------------------------
// Under partition=blocks2d(i,j):
//   - a is indexed [i][k]: dim 0 partition-covered (by i), dim 1
//     not (k is not partitioned). Coverage forms a contiguous
//     prefix {0} → bounds = [(i, i_band)]. wait_slice slices a
//     by leading-axis (correct).
//   - c is indexed [i][j]: dim 0 covered (i), dim 1 covered (j).
//     Contiguous prefix {0, 1} → bounds = [(i, i_band), (j, j_band)].
//     wait_slice's 2D row-loop slice-paste (TASK-0294) handles the
//     gather correctly.
//   - b is indexed [k][j]: dim 0 NOT covered (k is not partitioned),
//     dim 1 covered (j). Coverage {1} is NOT a contiguous prefix
//     starting at dim 0. Pre-TASK-0302 the TASK-0301 per-symbol
//     filter would have emitted bounds = [(j, j_band)] (j IS in b's
//     observed union), which wait_slice would silently mis-map to
//     b's k dimension. TASK-0302's dim-prefix check detects the
//     sparse coverage and drops to empty bounds → wait_slice
//     whole-array broadcast of b (over-transfer but bit-correct).
//
// Why sync transfers
// ------------------
// Sync-only schedule lowers on every tier-1 backend without
// capability gaps. Async variants are out of scope for this cell.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    place load_a on host;
    place load_b on host;
    place save_c on host;
    place madd   on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // 2x2-grid partition over the (i, j) nest. N=16 → 8×8 tile per
    // worker. The partition_blocks2d pass pairs i (outer) with the
    // first inner Repeat (j) and writes both bands into
    // partition_worker_ranges; the k-loop (innermost reduction)
    // remains intact per-worker.
    loop i : partition=blocks2d;

    transfer a : sync;
    transfer b : sync;
    transfer c : sync;
}
